        "# Interpreted\n",
        "\n",
        "Python is commonly called an interpreted language because an interpreter executes its programs. In CPython, source is typically compiled to bytecode before execution.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-interpreted)"
      ]
